# Python and Text Quality

All Python files must be normal multi-line source files.

Do not write compressed single-line Python files.

Each import should be on a normal line.

Each class should use normal indentation.

Each function should use normal indentation.

Each method should use normal indentation.

Do not put an entire module on one line.

Markdown files must also be normal multi-line text.

Do not compress Markdown into one long line.

Do not introduce hidden Unicode characters.

Do not introduce bidirectional Unicode control characters.

Avoid special arrows and unusual invisible characters.

Prefer plain ASCII punctuation in rules and code.

Keep line length reasonable.

Target maximum line length is below 140 characters.

After editing Python files, run python -m pytest.

Before submitting, check that edited files have reasonable line counts.
